# night_voices.pdl - the voices of the NIGHT class cast (2026-10-23, claude, from the owner's request: "try to get the old voices back: tomom = japanese woman, maxine = english young girl, rahweh = british young man; and save those voice profiles").
# Read by convert_night_cast.py (this folder). The same four profiles are VOICE2 rows (ids tomom / maxine / rahweh / narrator) in the voice-fx studio's state/voices2.pdl, so the studio lists and edits them; the studio's numbers and these numbers must stay the same.
# NIGHTVOICE | CAST NAME | kokoro voice | kokoro lang | pitch (semitones) | formant (semitone-equivalents) | bright dB | warm dB | studio base (edge name in @.apps/pet-trainer/voices.pdl KMAP) | note
# MEASURED, NOT HEARD: median F0 of one sample sentence per profile (autocorrelation, on debil, 2026-10-23): tomom 255 Hz, maxine 231 Hz (219 Hz at pitch +3), rahweh 163 Hz, narrator 122 Hz. The raw Kokoro voices: jf_alpha 255, bf_lily 205, bm_george 141, bm_fable 132. Whether they SOUND like "a Japanese woman / a young English girl / a young British man" is the owner's ear to judge: change the numbers in the studio (voice-fx) and in this file, nothing else.
# History: the first NIGHT classes used edge-tts voices (MAXINE en-GB-MaisieNeural, TOMO zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural, RAHWEH zh-CN-YunxiaNeural, NARRATOR zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural per the script headers). edge-tts has returned HTTP 403 since 2026-10-12, so the NIGHT 45 to 51 audio used the stand-ins in convert_night_to_audio_remote.py (bf_emma, af_heart, am_michael, bm_george). These rows replace those stand-ins for new classes; old classes are not re-rendered.
NIGHTVOICE | MAXINE       | bf_lily  | en-gb | 4  | 2.5  | 2 | 0 | en-GB-MaisieNeural      | English young girl: Kokoro British girl voice (the studio's existing Maisie mapping), raised pitch and a smaller vocal tract
NIGHTVOICE | TOMO         | jf_alpha | en-us | -1 | -0.5 | 0 | 1 | ja-JP-NanamiNeural-en   | Japanese woman: Kokoro's Japanese voice made to speak English text (KMAP alias ja-JP-NanamiNeural-en, lang en-us). The accent is whatever the voice carries; unverified by ear. Alternatives to try in the studio: jf_gongitsune (231 Hz, calmer), jf_nezumi (253 Hz)
NIGHTVOICE | RAHWEH       | bm_george| en-gb | 2  | 1.0  | 0 | 0 | en-GB-RyanNeural        | British young man: Kokoro British male voice raised two semitones, slightly smaller vocal tract. Alternatives: bm_daniel (125 Hz), bm_lewis (102 Hz, deeper)
NIGHTVOICE | THE NARRATOR | bm_fable | en-gb | 0  | -0.5 | 0 | 2 | en-GB-FableNeural       | storyteller: Kokoro bm_fable, a little warmer and a little larger vocal tract, so he is not confused with Rahweh
